{"status":"completed","agent":"agent-one","method":"Compile each preserved Haskell source separately with the identical Replay adapter. Run 14 public-only expanding-prefix historical single-decision episodes at t=39..52. At t use only bars 0..t, evaluate signal, buy if enabled at next close t+1, then mark at t+7. Also calculate the exact original 60-bar signal without inventing unavailable forward outcomes. OLD and NEW are retained-identical.","limitations":["AGENT-REPORTED offline evidence only; not independently verified improvement or judge settlement.","Only the 60 already-published round-0 bars were used. There are no public future labels after t=59, so the exact 60-bar deployment signal has no offline forward P&L test.","Historical proxy cases use causal prefixes of 40 through 53 bars, not the deployment main's enforced 60-bar input; fit anchors remain 7,15,20,30. OLD and NEW use identical prefixes, costs, fill and mark settings.","Replay imports each preserved source's actual fit and split and mirrors its unchanged sizing/forecast/gating expressions; submission main is not invoked because it writes orders. This tests the numerical strategy core, not submission-file I/O.","These overlapping seven-bar historical episodes share labels and are not independent observations. They reuse public data previously available at strategy design time, are exploratory rather than genuinely held-out, and do not estimate deployment significance.","Each episode independently starts with cash 1000 and zero units; metrics are means across episodes, not cumulative or compounded portfolio profit. Buy-hold buys at each episode's same next close and marks at t+7; cash is zero profit.","No exit is simulated: end-of-episode holdings are marked to raw close, exactly as the public brief specifies. Buy fee and slippage are charged; sell fee/slippage are specified but not applied to a mark.","A six-residual-standard-deviation reserve is statistical rather than a guarantee. No observed repl